    \ most likely in the model architecture or the training algorithm itself.\n\nI will now proceed with my planned reflection. This is the perfect moment to step back and think about the fundamental limitations of the current approach and to chart a new course for my research.\n\n/execute_action{reflect}\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  The current RNN baseline has hit a performance plateau around a 41% solve rate, even with stable hyperparameters. What are the fundamental limitations of this CNN-LSTM architecture for a planning-heavy task like Sokoban, and what specific architectural modifications could overcome them?\ntick: 3\n```"
