tick: 18
role: model
parts:
- text: "My reflection is complete. I have a clear hypothesis and a concrete plan to overcome the performance plateau of the current SOTA. The fundamental flaw is the destruction of spatial information by the flatten-and-process architecture. My next experiment will replace the standard LSTM with a Convolutional LSTM (ConvLSTM) to maintain and leverage this crucial spatial context throughout the network.\n\nI will now return to the Research Counter to implement and submit this new architecture.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Architectural Change: CNN + ConvLSTM\"\ntags: \"convlstm, architecture, spatial reasoning, planning\"\nabstract: \"This submission tests a new architecture to overcome the performance plateau of the CNN-LSTM baseline. It replaces the standard LSTM with a Convolutional LSTM (ConvLSTM). The hypothesis is that by maintaining a 2D spatial hidden state, the ConvLSTM can better reason about the geometric relationships in Sokoban,\
    \ which are lost when the CNN's feature maps are flattened for a standard LSTM. This experiment uses the stable hyperparameters from ID 15 to isolate the architectural impact.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  A new architecture using a Convolutional LSTM (ConvLSTM) to preserve spatial reasoning.\n  This replaces the standard LSTM from the baseline, aiming to break the performance plateau.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Use fixed, stable hyperparameters from experiment ID 15 to isolate architectural impact.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([0.000511]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.010218]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.403564]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\
    \ # Features for the ConvLSTM hidden state\n      }\n\n  class ConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A Convolutional LSTM cell.\"\"\"\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int, int] = (3, 3)\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          c, h = carry\n          # Combined convolutions for input, forget, cell, and output gates\n          conv_all = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.features * 4,\n              kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform()\n          )\n          \n          # Apply convolution to concatenated input and hidden state\n          i_f_g_o = conv_all(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          \n          # Split into individual gates\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(i_f_g_o, 4, axis=-1)\n          \n          # Apply activations\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i)\n          f = nn.sigmoid(f)\n          g = nn.tanh(g)\n          o = nn.sigmoid(o)\n    \
    \      \n          # Calculate new cell and hidden states\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * nn.tanh(new_c)\n          \n          return (new_c, new_h), new_h\n\n  class CNNConvLSTM(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"CNN feature extractor followed by a ConvLSTM for spatial-temporal reasoning.\"\"\"\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          cnn_output_shape = (x.shape[1], x.shape[2], self.conv_lstm_features) # H, W, C\n          \n          # Initialize RNN state if not provided\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size,) + cnn_output_shape),\n                  'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size,) + cnn_output_shape),\n              }\n          \n          # Reset states\
    \ for episodes that are done\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1, 1, 1) # Reshape for spatial state\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'c': rnn_state['c'] * (1 - done_mask),\n                  'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask),\n              }\n          \n          # --- CNN Feature Extractor (identical to baseline) ---\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3,\
    \ 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv4_in\n          cnn_features = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # --- ConvLSTM Layer ---\n          conv_lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCell(features=self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), conv_lstm_out = conv_lstm_cell((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), cnn_features)\n          \n          # --- MLP Heads ---\n          # Flatten the spatial output from the ConvLSTM\n          x = conv_lstm_out.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          \n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      \"\"\"Create the CNN-ConvLSTM network.\"\"\"\n      return CNNConvLSTM(\n          conv_lstm_features=int(hparams['conv_lstm_features']),\n\
    \          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2'])\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**My Current Thinking: Implementing ConvLSTM for Enhanced Spatial Reasoning**\n\nMy reflection is complete. I've concluded that the standard LSTM in the current baseline is limiting its ability to plan effectively due to the flattening of spatial information. My plan is to replace it with a Convolutional LSTM (ConvLSTM) to preserve this crucial spatial structure. To that end, I'll now head to the Research Counter and submit a new experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Architectural Change: CNN + ConvLSTM\"\ntags: [\"convlstm\", \"rnn\", \"architecture\", \"spatial reasoning\"]\nabstract: |\n  This experiment explores a novel architecture to address the limitations of the current RNN baseline.  The hypothesis is that integrating a ConvLSTM layer, which inherently maintains spatial information, will outperform the baseline LSTM in tasks requiring spatial reasoning. The model architecture uses the baseline CNN feature\
  \ extractor, but the flattening LSTM layer is replaced by a ConvLSTM layer, and the final MLP heads remain the same.  Hyperparameters are fixed to those from a stable run (ID 15) to isolate the architectural change.\ncontent: |\n    import flax.linen as nn\n    import jax\n    import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n    class ConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n        features: int\n        kernel_size: int\n        recurrent_kernel_initializer: str = \"orthogonal\"\n        kernel_initializer: str = \"orthogonal\"\n\n        @nn.compact\n        def __call__(self, h_prev, c_prev, x):\n            # Input to hidden\n            i = nn.Conv(\n                features=self.features * 4,\n                kernel_size=(self.kernel_size, self.kernel_size),\n                use_bias=True,\n                kernel_init=nn.initializers.orthogonal(),\n                name=\"i\",\n            )(x)\n            # Hidden to hidden\n            h = nn.Conv(\n                features=self.features * 4,\n                kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,\
  \ self.kernel_size),\n                use_bias=False,\n                kernel_init=nn.initializers.orthogonal(),\n                name=\"h\",\n            )(h_prev)\n            # Combine input and hidden\n            gate_inputs = i + h\n\n            # Gate activations\n            i, f, c, o = jnp.split(gate_inputs, 4, axis=-1)\n\n            # Cell state update\n            new_c = (\n                f * c_prev + i * nn.tanh(c)\n            )  # LSTM: f_t * c_{t-1} + i_t * tanh(C_t)\n            # New hidden state\n            new_h = o * nn.tanh(new_c)\n\n            return new_h, new_c\n\n    class CNNConvLSTM(nn.Module):\n        cnn_features_2: int = 64\n        conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n        action_dim: int = 18\n\n        @nn.compact\n        def __call__(self, x, rnn_state, done):\n            # CNN feature extractor - same as baseline\n            x = nn.Conv(features=32, kernel_size=(8, 8), strides=4, name=\"conv1\")(x)\n            x = nn.relu(x)\n            x = nn.Conv(features=64,\
  \ kernel_size=(4, 4), strides=2, name=\"conv2\")(x)\n            x = nn.relu(x)\n            x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), strides=1, name=\"conv3\")(x)\n            x = nn.relu(x)\n\n            # ConvLSTM input: (B, H, W, C_cnn)\n            # Initialize hidden and cell states if they are None (start of episode)\n            if rnn_state is None or done:\n                batch_size = x.shape[0]\n                hidden_shape = (\n                    batch_size,\n                    x.shape[1],\n                    x.shape[2],\n                    self.conv_lstm_features,\n                )\n                rnn_state = (\n                    jnp.zeros(hidden_shape),  # hidden state\n                    jnp.zeros(hidden_shape),  # cell state\n                )\n\n            h_prev, c_prev = rnn_state\n\n            # Apply ConvLSTM\n            h, c = ConvLSTMCell(\n                features=self.conv"
