tick: 22
role: model
parts:
- text: "My reflection is complete, and the results from my hyperparameter search on the ConvLSTM (ID 27) have arrived.\n\n**Experiment Analysis (ID 27):**\n*   **Hypothesis:** Tuning the hyperparameters for the new ConvLSTM architecture would further improve its score.\n*   **Result:** The mean score is 54.9, a slight decrease from the untuned ConvLSTM's score of 55.7.\n*   **Observation:** The model remains extremely stable (Std: 0.008). This indicates that the ConvLSTM architecture is inherently robust. The hyperparameter search did not yield an improvement, suggesting that the initial parameters were already near-optimal or that the architecture is not highly sensitive to these specific parameters within this stable range.\n\n**Conclusion & Plan:**\nThis result reinforces the conclusion from my reflection: the next major bottleneck is not the architecture or its hyperparameters, but the learning algorithm itself. Having confirmed the robustness of the ConvLSTM, I am now confident in\
    \ using it as the testbed for a more advanced training algorithm.\n\nMy plan, as formulated in the reflection chamber, is to implement Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO). I will now return to the Research Counter to implement a custom `training_step` with the PPO clipped surrogate objective and submit it.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Algorithmic Change: PPO with ConvLSTM\"\ntags: \"ppo, policy gradient, algorithm, convlstm, stability\"\nabstract: \"This experiment shifts focus from architectural changes to algorithmic improvements. It replaces the default policy gradient training step with a Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) implementation, featuring a clipped surrogate objective. The hypothesis is that PPO will provide more stable and efficient policy updates, leading to a higher score. The successful ConvLSTM architecture (ID 22) is used as the base model, with the new training step being the only variable.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\
    \"\n  Implementation of Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) to train the ConvLSTM architecture.\n  This introduces a custom, more robust training_step.\n  \"\"\"\n  \n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  # Use the best-performing, stable hyperparameters from the ConvLSTM experiments.\n  # Add a new hyperparameter for the PPO clipping.\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([0.000511]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.010218]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.403564]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]), # PPO clipping parameter\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  # --- ConvLSTM Architecture (Identical to previous successful experiment) ---\n  class ConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n\
    \      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int, int] = (3, 3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          c, h = carry\n          conv_all = nn.Conv(features=self.features * 4, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')\n          i_f_g_o = conv_all(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(i_f_g_o, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n          g = nn.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * nn.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_c, new_h), new_h\n\n  class CNNConvLSTM(nn.Module):\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state):\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          cnn_output_shape = (x.shape[1], x.shape[2], self.conv_lstm_features)\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size,) + cnn_output_shape), 'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size,)\
    \ + cnn_output_shape)}\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1, 1, 1)\n              rnn_state = {'c': rnn_state['c'] * (1 - done_mask), 'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask)}\n          \n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          res_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x += res_in; x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          res_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x += res_in\n          cnn_features = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          carry,\
    \ conv_lstm_out = ConvLSTMCell(features=self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), cnn_features)\n          rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h'] = carry\n          \n          x = conv_lstm_out.reshape((batch_size, -1)); x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTM(\n          conv_lstm_features=int(hparams['conv_lstm_features']),\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']))\n          \n  # --- Custom PPO Training Step ---\n  # Re-importing necessary libraries for the self-contained function\n  from jax import vmap, lax\n  from system.defaults import default_calculate_gae\n\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      observations = batch['observations']\n\
    \      actions = batch['actions']\n      rewards = batch['rewards']\n      dones = batch['dones']\n      old_log_probs = batch['log_probs']\n      old_values = batch['values']\n      final_values = batch['final_values']\n      initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n      \n      advantages = default_calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n      returns = advantages + old_values\n      \n      batch_size, trajectory_length = observations.shape[:2]\n\n      def loss_fn(params):\n          def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n              env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), initial_rnn_states)\n              def step_fn(carry, t):\n                  obs, prev_done = observations[env_idx, t], jnp.where(t > 0, dones[env_idx, t-1], False)\n                  logits_batched, value_batched, new_rnn_state_batched = network.apply(params, obs[None, ...], prev_done[None, ...], jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[None,\
    \ ...], carry))\n                  return jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[0], new_rnn_state_batched), (logits_batched[0], value_batched[0])\n              _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(trajectory_length))\n              return env_logits, env_values\n          all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch_size))\n          \n          log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          action_indices = jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None], jnp.arange(trajectory_length), actions\n          new_log_probs = log_probs_all[action_indices]\n          \n          # PPO-specific calculation\n          ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - old_log_probs)\n          advantages_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n          clip_epsilon = hparams['clip_epsilon']\n          \n          policy_loss1 = ratio * advantages_detached\n          policy_loss2 = jnp.clip(ratio, 1.0 - clip_epsilon, 1.0 + clip_epsilon) * advantages_detached\n\
    \          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(policy_loss1, policy_loss2))\n          \n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)) ** 2)\n          \n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n          \n          total_loss = policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n          return total_loss\n\n      loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      return params, opt_state\n```"
