tick: 27
role: model
parts:
- text: "My reflection is complete. I have identified the next major bottleneck: the low-level nature of the observation space. My new plan is to engineer additional feature channels that make local spatial relationships explicit, thereby aiding the network's planning capabilities.\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter to implement this feature engineering approach and submit it as my next experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Feature Engineering for Spatial Reasoning\"\ntags: \"feature engineering, spatial reasoning, convlstm, ppo\"\nabstract: \"This experiment addresses the performance plateau by enriching the observation space. Instead of feeding raw one-hot encoded grids to the network, this submission adds new feature channels that explicitly encode local spatial relationships, such as identifying 'pushable' boxes. The hypothesis is that this engineered input will reduce the network's burden of learning these fundamental relationships\
    \ from scratch, freeing its capacity for higher-level planning and breaking the current performance ceiling.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Feature engineering to enhance the observation space for the ConvLSTM+PPO agent.\n  \"\"\"\n  \n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([0.000511]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.010218]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.403564]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  @jax.jit\n  def engineer_features(obs):\n      \"\"\"Adds new feature channels to the observation.\"\"\"\n      # Original channels: 0: empty, 1: wall, 2: target, 3: agent, 4: box, 5: agent_on_target,\
    \ 6: box_on_target, 7: time\n      agent_ch = obs[..., 3] + obs[..., 5]\n      box_ch = obs[..., 4] + obs[..., 6]\n      \n      # --- Create \"Pushable Box\" channel ---\n      # A box is pushable if an agent is adjacent to it.\n      # Use convolution with a cross kernel to find adjacencies.\n      kernel = jnp.array([[0, 1, 0], [1, 0, 1], [0, 1, 0]])[..., None, None]\n      agent_neighbors = jax.scipy.signal.convolve(agent_ch[None, ..., None], kernel, mode='same')[0, ..., 0]\n      pushable_box_ch = box_ch * (agent_neighbors > 0)\n      \n      # Concatenate the new channel\n      new_obs = jnp.concatenate([obs, pushable_box_ch[..., None]], axis=-1)\n      return new_obs\n      \n  # --- PPO Training Step Modified to Use Feature Engineering ---\n  from jax import vmap, lax\n  from storage.system.defaults import default_calculate_gae\n\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      # Apply feature engineering to the batch of observations\n     \
    \ # vmap the engineer_features function over the batch and time dimensions\n      engineered_obs = vmap(vmap(engineer_features))(batch['observations'])\n      \n      advantages = default_calculate_gae(batch['rewards'], batch['values'], batch['dones'], next_values=batch['final_values'])\n      returns = advantages + batch['values']\n      \n      batch_size, trajectory_length = engineered_obs.shape[:2]\n\n      def loss_fn(params):\n          def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n              env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), batch['initial_rnn_states'])\n              def step_fn(carry, t):\n                  obs, prev_done = engineered_obs[env_idx, t], jnp.where(t > 0, batch['dones'][env_idx, t-1], False)\n                  logits_batched, value_batched, new_rnn_state_batched = network.apply(params, obs[None, ...], prev_done[None, ...], jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[None, ...], carry))\n                  return jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[0], new_rnn_state_batched),\
    \ (logits_batched[0], value_batched[0])\n              _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(trajectory_length))\n              return env_logits, env_values\n          all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch_size))\n          \n          log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          action_indices = jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None], jnp.arange(trajectory_length), batch['actions']\n          new_log_probs = log_probs_all[action_indices]\n          \n          ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - batch['log_probs'])\n          advantages_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n          clip_epsilon = hparams['clip_epsilon']\n          \n          policy_loss1 = ratio * advantages_detached\n          policy_loss2 = jnp.clip(ratio, 1.0 - clip_epsilon, 1.0 + clip_epsilon) * advantages_detached\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(policy_loss1, policy_loss2))\n          \n          value_loss\
    \ = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)) ** 2)\n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n          \n          total_loss = policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n          return total_loss\n\n      loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      return params, opt_state\n\n  # --- ConvLSTM Architecture (Modified to accept more input channels) ---\n  class ConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int, int] = (3, 3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          c, h = carry\n          conv_all = nn.Conv(features=self.features * 4, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')\n          i_f_g_o = conv_all(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n  \
    \        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(i_f_g_o, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n          g = nn.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * nn.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_c, new_h), new_h\n\n  class CNNConvLSTM(nn.Module):\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          # Apply feature engineering at the network level as well for initialization and single-step calls\n          x_engineered = engineer_features(x[0])[None, ...] # Process single item in batch, then add batch dim back\n          \n          batch_size = x_engineered.shape[0]\n          cnn_output_shape = (x_engineered.shape[1], x_engineered.shape[2], self.conv_lstm_features)\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size,) + cnn_output_shape), 'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size,) + cnn_output_shape)}\n   \
    \       if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1, 1, 1)\n              rnn_state = {'c': rnn_state['c'] * (1 - done_mask), 'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask)}\n          \n          # Use the engineered observation from now on\n          x = x_engineered\n          \n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          res_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x += res_in; x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          res_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x +=\
    \ res_in\n          cnn_features = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          carry, conv_lstm_out = ConvLSTMCell(features=self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), cnn_features)\n          rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h'] = carry\n          \n          x = conv_lstm_out.reshape((batch_size, -1)); x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTM(\n          conv_lstm_features=int(hparams['conv_lstm_features']),\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']))\n```"
