- text: "My ICM experiment failed. I must analyze the error.\n\n**Error Analysis (ID 66):**\n*   **Error:** `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'init'`.\n*   **Location:** The error occurs in the system's validation script when it calls `network.init(...)`. The `network` object is `None`.\n*   **Root Cause:** My `create_network` function has a `pass` statement, so it returns `None`. I was so focused on the conceptual complexity of the ICM that I submitted placeholder code for the core functions. This is a severe and embarrassing oversight.\n\n**Conclusion & Plan:**\nThis failure is entirely due to my own carelessness. I cannot submit conceptual placeholders. I must provide a full, working implementation. I will now write the complete code for the ICM experiment. This will involve:\n\n1.  **A single `TrainState`:** Instead of separate networks and optimizers, I'll use a single JAX `TrainState` to manage the parameters and optimizer states for both the policy network and the\
    \ ICM. This is a cleaner, more standard approach.\n2.  **A unified `Network` class:** I will create a single `MasterNet` class that contains both the policy network (`CNNConvLSTM`) and the `ICM` as sub-modules. This simplifies parameter management.\n3.  **A complete `training_step`:** I will fully implement the logic for calculating intrinsic rewards, combining losses, and updating all parameters.\n\n**Plan:**\n1.  Document this careless failure.\n2.  Implement the full, correct version of the ICM experiment.\n3.  Resubmit.\n\nFirst, I will go to my private memory to log this failure.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Experiment Log 11: ICM Failure (Placeholder Code)\"\ncontent: |\n  **Experiment ID:** 66\n  **Title:** Exploration: Intrinsic Curiosity Module (ICM)\n  **Result:** Failed (n.a.) due to a code error.\n\n  **Error Analysis:**\n  This failure was caused by a critical oversight. In my haste to outline the complex ICM logic,\
    \ I submitted placeholder code with key functions like `create_network` and `training_step` left incomplete. The system rightfully failed when it could not initialize a `None` network.\n\n  **Conclusion & Fix:**\n  This is a serious process error. I must ensure all submissions are complete and runnable. I will now write the full implementation for the ICM experiment, using a unified training state and a master network class to manage the policy and ICM components cleanly.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Exploration: Intrinsic Curiosity Module (ICM) (v2)\"\ntags: \"exploration, curiosity, icm, ppo, convlstm, bugfix\"\nabstract: \"This is a corrected and complete implementation of the Intrinsic Curiosity Module (ICM) experiment, fixing the placeholder code bug from ID 66. The ICM generates a novelty-based reward to guide exploration. The hypothesis is that this more intelligent exploration strategy will overcome the current performance\
    \ plateau by enabling the agent to discover more complex solutions.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Full implementation of an Intrinsic Curiosity Module (ICM) for Sokoban.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax, optax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from flax.training.train_state import TrainState\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from jax import vmap, lax\n  from storage.system.defaults import default_calculate_gae\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'icm_beta': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'icm_eta': tune.choice([0.01]), # Intrinsic reward scaling factor\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'feature_space_dim':\
    \ tune.choice([256]),\n      }\n\n  # --- Agent and ICM Networks ---\n  class CNNConvLSTM(nn.Module): # Identical to previous successful versions\n      conv_lstm_features: int; cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          cnn_output_shape = (x.shape[1], x.shape[2], self.conv_lstm_features)\n          if rnn_state is None: rnn_state = {'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size,) + cnn_output_shape), 'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size,) + cnn_output_shape)}\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1, 1, 1)\n              rnn_state = {'c': rnn_state['c']*(1-done_mask), 'h': rnn_state['h']*(1-done_mask)}\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          res_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1,\
    \ kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x += res_in; x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          res_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x += res_in\n          cnn_features = nn.relu(x)\n          carry, conv_lstm_out = nn.scan(nn.LSTMCell, variable_broadcast='params', split_rngs={'params': False}, length=1, in_axes=1, out_axes=1)((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), cnn_features.reshape(batch_size, 1, -1))\n          rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h'] = carry\n          x = conv_lstm_out.reshape((batch_size, -1)); x = nn.Dense(256)(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          return nn.Dense(4)(x), nn.Dense(1)(x).squeeze(-1), rnn_state\n\n  class ICM(nn.Module):\n      feature_space_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, obs_t, obs_t_plus_1,\
    \ action_t):\n          def encode(x):\n              x = nn.Conv(32, (3,3), (2,2), 'SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n              x = nn.Conv(32, (3,3), (2,2), 'SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n              return nn.Dense(self.feature_space_dim)(x.reshape((x.shape[0], -1)))\n          phi_t, phi_t_plus_1 = encode(obs_t), encode(obs_t_plus_1)\n          \n          # Inverse Model\n          inverse_input = jnp.concatenate([phi_t, phi_t_plus_1],-1)\n          pred_action_logits = nn.Dense(4)(nn.relu(nn.Dense(256)(inverse_input)))\n          \n          # Forward Model\n          action_one_hot = jax.nn.one_hot(action_t, 4)\n          forward_input = jnp.concatenate([phi_t, action_one_hot], -1)\n          pred_phi_t_plus_1 = nn.Dense(self.feature_space_dim)(nn.relu(nn.Dense(256)(forward_input)))\n          return pred_action_logits, pred_phi_t_plus_1, phi_t_plus_1\n\n  class MasterNet(nn.Module):\n      conv_lstm_features: int; cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; feature_space_dim: int\n\
    \      def setup(self):\n          self.agent = CNNConvLSTM(self.conv_lstm_features, self.cnn_features_1, self.cnn_features_2)\n          self.icm = ICM(self.feature_space_dim)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return MasterNet(hparams['conv_lstm_features'], hparams['cnn_features_1'], hparams['cnn_features_2'], hparams['feature_space_dim'])\n\n  # --- Training Step ---\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      obs, actions, rewards, dones, old_log_probs, old_values = batch['observations'], batch['actions'], batch['rewards'], batch['dones'], batch['log_probs'], batch['values']\n      \n      # Calculate Intrinsic Reward\n      obs_t = obs[:, :-1].reshape(-1, *obs.shape[2:])\n      obs_t_plus_1 = obs[:, 1:].reshape(-1, *obs.shape[2:])\n      actions_t = actions[:, :-1].reshape(-1)\n      _, pred_phi, true_phi = network.apply({'params': params}, obs_t=obs_t, obs_t_plus_1=obs_t_plus_1, action_t=actions_t, method=lambda module, *args, **kwargs:\
    \ module.icm(*args, **kwargs))\n      intrinsic_reward = jnp.mean((pred_phi - true_phi)**2, axis=-1).reshape(actions.shape[0], -1)\n      total_rewards = rewards[:,:-1] + hparams['icm_eta'] * jax.lax.stop_gradient(intrinsic_reward)\n      \n      # GAE with combined rewards\n      advantages = default_calculate_gae(jnp.pad(total_rewards, ((0,0),(0,1))), old_values, dones, next_values=batch['final_values'])\n      returns = advantages + old_values\n      \n      def loss_fn(params):\n          # Agent PPO Loss\n          def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n              env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), batch['initial_rnn_states'])\n              def step_fn(carry, t):\n                  logits, value, new_state = network.apply({'params': params}, obs[env_idx,t][None,...], jnp.where(t>0,dones[env_idx,t-1],False)[None,...], jax.tree.map(lambda y:y[None,...], carry), method=lambda module, *args, **kwargs: module.agent(*args, **kwargs))\n           \
    \       return jax.tree.map(lambda y:y[0], new_state), (logits[0], value[0])\n              _,(logits,values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(obs.shape[1]))\n              return logits, values\n          all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(obs.shape[0]))\n          log_probs_all = nn.log_softmax(all_logits)\n          new_log_probs = jnp.take_along_axis(log_probs_all, actions[...,None],-1).squeeze(-1)\n          ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - old_log_probs)\n          advantages_detached = lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n          ppo_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(ratio*advantages_detached, jnp.clip(ratio, 1-hparams['clip_epsilon'], 1+hparams['clip_epsilon'])*advantages_detached))\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - lax.stop_gradient(returns))**2)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(nn.softmax(all_logits) * log_probs_all, -1))\n          agent_loss = ppo_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef']*value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef']*entropy\n\
    \          \n          # ICM Loss\n          pred_action_logits, pred_phi, true_phi = network.apply({'params': params}, obs_t=obs_t, obs_t_plus_1=obs_t_plus_1, action_t=actions_t, method=lambda module, *args, **kwargs: module.icm(*args, **kwargs))\n          inverse_loss = optax.softmax_cross_entropy_with_integer_labels(pred_action_logits, actions_t).mean()\n          forward_loss = jnp.mean((pred_phi - lax.stop_gradient(true_phi))**2)\n          icm_loss = (1-hparams['icm_beta'])*inverse_loss + hparams['icm_beta']*forward_loss\n          \n          return agent_loss + icm_loss\n\n      grads = jax.grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      return params, opt_state\n```"
