tick: 39
role: model
parts:
- text: "My ICM experiment has failed again. This string of implementation failures is a serious problem.\n\n**Error Analysis (ID 68):**\n*   **Error:** `AttributeError: \"MasterNet\" object has no attribute \"__call__\"`.\n*   **Root Cause:** The system's validation harness tries to initialize the network with `network.init(...)`. Flax models are typically initialized via their `__call__` method. My `MasterNet` class correctly uses a `setup` method to define its sub-modules (`agent` and `icm`), but it lacks a `__call__` method to define the default forward pass. The system doesn't know what to do when it tries to use the `MasterNet`.\n\n**The Fix:**\nI need to define a `__call__` method in `MasterNet`. This method should, by default, just call the agent's forward pass, as this is the primary function needed for action selection during data collection. The ICM's methods can be called explicitly within the `training_step`.\n\n**Plan:**\n1.  Document this embarrassing and repeated pattern\
    \ of failure. I am being careless.\n2.  Fix the `MasterNet` class by adding a `__call__` method that delegates to the `self.agent` sub-module.\n3.  Resubmit the experiment. I must get this working to test my exploration hypothesis.\n\nFirst, to my private memory to log this failure.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Experiment Log 12: ICM Failure (Missing __call__)\"\ncontent: |\n  **Experiment ID:** 68\n  **Title:** Exploration: Intrinsic Curiosity Module (ICM) (v2)\n  **Result:** Failed (n.a.) due to a code error.\n\n  **Error Analysis:**\n  This is my third failure attempting to implement the ICM. The error was an `AttributeError` because my main network class, `MasterNet`, was missing a `__call__` method. The system's initialization procedure relies on this method to trace and build the network parameters. My design of separating the agent and ICM was correct, but the container class was incomplete.\n\n  **Conclusion & Fix:**\n\
    \  This pattern of basic implementation errors is unacceptable and is wasting valuable station time. I need to be more thorough. I will add the required `__call__` method to the `MasterNet` class, which will simply pass its inputs to the agent sub-module. This will allow the network to initialize correctly.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Exploration: Intrinsic Curiosity Module (ICM) (v3)\"\ntags: \"exploration, curiosity, icm, ppo, convlstm, bugfix\"\nabstract: \"This is the third and hopefully final implementation of the ICM experiment, fixing a critical bug from ID 68 where the master network class was missing a `__call__` method for initialization. The scientific hypothesis that curiosity-driven exploration can break the current performance plateau remains the core of this submission.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Final, corrected implementation of an Intrinsic Curiosity Module (ICM) for Sokoban.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax, optax\n\
    \  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from jax import vmap, lax\n  from storage.system.defaults import default_calculate_gae\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'icm_beta': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'icm_eta': tune.choice([0.01]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'feature_space_dim': tune.choice([256]),\n      }\n\n  # --- Agent and ICM Networks ---\n  class CNNConvLSTM(nn.Module):\n      conv_lstm_features: int; cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          batch_size =\
    \ x.shape[0]\n          cnn_output_shape = (x.shape[1], x.shape[2], self.conv_lstm_features)\n          if rnn_state is None: rnn_state = {'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size,) + cnn_output_shape), 'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size,) + cnn_output_shape)}\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1, 1, 1)\n              rnn_state = {'c': rnn_state['c']*(1-done_mask), 'h': rnn_state['h']*(1-done_mask)}\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          res_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x += res_in; x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          res_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x += res_in\n\
    \          cnn_features = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          (new_c, new_h), _ = nn.LSTMCell()((rnn_state['c'].mean(axis=(1,2)), rnn_state['h'].mean(axis=(1,2))), cnn_features.reshape(batch_size, -1))\n          rnn_state = {'c': jnp.broadcast_to(new_c[:, None, None, :], rnn_state['c'].shape), 'h': jnp.broadcast_to(new_h[:, None, None, :], rnn_state['h'].shape)}\n          \n          x = new_h; x = nn.Dense(256)(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          return nn.Dense(4)(x), nn.Dense(1)(x).squeeze(-1), rnn_state\n\n  class ICM(nn.Module):\n      feature_space_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, obs_t, obs_t_plus_1, action_t):\n          def encode(x):\n              x = nn.Conv(32, (3,3), (2,2), 'SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n              x = nn.Conv(32, (3,3), (2,2), 'SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n              return nn.Dense(self.feature_space_dim)(x.reshape((x.shape[0], -1)))\n          phi_t, phi_t_plus_1 = encode(obs_t), encode(obs_t_plus_1)\n          inverse_input = jnp.concatenate([phi_t,\
    \ phi_t_plus_1], -1)\n          pred_action_logits = nn.Dense(4)(nn.relu(nn.Dense(256)(inverse_input)))\n          action_one_hot = jax.nn.one_hot(action_t, 4)\n          forward_input = jnp.concatenate([phi_t, action_one_hot], -1)\n          pred_phi_t_plus_1 = nn.Dense(self.feature_space_dim)(nn.relu(nn.Dense(256)(forward_input)))\n          return pred_action_logits, pred_phi_t_plus_1, phi_t_plus_1\n\n  class MasterNet(nn.Module):\n      conv_lstm_features: int; cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; feature_space_dim: int\n      def setup(self):\n          self.agent = CNNConvLSTM(self.conv_lstm_features, self.cnn_features_1, self.cnn_features_2)\n          self.icm = ICM(self.feature_space_dim)\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          return self.agent(x, done, rnn_state)\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return MasterNet(\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'], cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], \n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\
    \ feature_space_dim=hparams['feature_space_dim'])\n\n  # --- Training Step ---\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      obs, actions, rewards, dones, old_log_probs, old_values = batch['observations'], batch['actions'], batch['rewards'], batch['dones'], batch['log_probs'], batch['values']\n      \n      obs_t = obs[:, :-1].reshape(-1, *obs.shape[2:])\n      obs_t_plus_1 = obs[:, 1:].reshape(-1, *obs.shape[2:])\n      actions_t = actions[:, :-1].reshape(-1)\n      _, pred_phi, true_phi = network.apply({'params': params}, obs_t, obs_t_plus_1, actions_t, method=lambda module, *a, **k: module.icm(*a, **k))\n      intrinsic_reward = jnp.mean((pred_phi - true_phi)**2, axis=-1).reshape(actions.shape[0], -1)\n      total_rewards = rewards[:,:-1] + hparams['icm_eta'] * jax.lax.stop_gradient(intrinsic_reward)\n      \n      advantages = default_calculate_gae(jnp.pad(total_rewards, ((0,0),(0,1))), old_values, dones, next_values=batch['final_values'])\n\
    \      returns = advantages + old_values\n      \n      def loss_fn(params):\n          def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n              env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), batch['initial_rnn_states'])\n              def step_fn(carry, t):\n                  logits, value, new_state = network.apply({'params': params}, obs[env_idx,t][None,...], jnp.where(t>0,dones[env_idx,t-1],False)[None,...], jax.tree.map(lambda y:y[None,...], carry))\n                  return jax.tree.map(lambda y:y[0], new_state), (logits[0], value[0])\n              _,(logits,values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(obs.shape[1]))\n              return logits, values\n          all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(obs.shape[0]))\n          log_probs_all = nn.log_softmax(all_logits)\n          new_log_probs = jnp.take_along_axis(log_probs_all, actions[...,None],-1).squeeze(-1)\n          ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - old_log_probs)\n \
    \         advantages_detached = lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n          ppo_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(ratio*advantages_detached, jnp.clip(ratio, 1-hparams['clip_epsilon'], 1+hparams['clip_epsilon'])*advantages_detached))\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - lax.stop_gradient(returns))**2)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(nn.softmax(all_logits) * log_probs_all, -1))\n          agent_loss = ppo_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef']*value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef']*entropy\n          \n          pred_action_logits, pred_phi, true_phi = network.apply({'params': params}, obs_t, obs_t_plus_1, actions_t, method=lambda module, *a, **k: module.icm(*a, **k))\n          inverse_loss = optax.softmax_cross_entropy_with_integer_labels(pred_action_logits, actions_t).mean()\n          forward_loss = jnp.mean((pred_phi - lax.stop_gradient(true_phi))**2)\n          icm_loss = (1-hparams['icm_beta'])*inverse_loss + hparams['icm_beta']*forward_loss\n          \n          return\
    \ agent_loss + icm_loss\n\n      grads = jax.grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      return params, opt_state\n```"
