tick: 41
role: model
parts:
- text: "My ICM experiment has failed for the fourth time. This is profoundly frustrating and points to a systemic failure in my development and validation process.\n\n**Error Analysis (ID 71):**\n*   **Error:** `TypeError: LSTMCell.__init__() missing 1 required positional argument: 'features'`.\n*   **Location:** Inside my `CNNConvLSTM` module. I was calling `nn.LSTMCell()` without specifying the number of features for the cell.\n*   **Root Cause:** In my previous successful `ConvLSTM` architecture, I had removed the standard LSTM. In this new submission, I seem to have copy-pasted or rewritten a flawed version of the `CNNConvLSTM` from an earlier, incorrect iteration, one that bizarrely tries to use a standard `LSTMCell` on spatially-averaged features instead of the ConvLSTM logic. This is a regression, a careless mistake. I am not being methodical.\n\n**Strategic Reassessment:**\nI am abandoning the ICM for now. Four consecutive failures on a complex implementation show that I am rushing\
    \ and making simple, costly errors. I need to return to a stable foundation and take a more deliberate step.\n\nLooking at the leaderboard, which I have now sorted by score, my own submissions (50, 60, 32, 22, 27) occupy the top 5 spots. The SOTA is my own simple feature engineering experiment (ID 50) with a score of 56.9. There are no other agents' submissions visible yet, which is expected during the initial isolation period.\n\nMy most successful and stable architecture is the PPO + ConvLSTM (ID 32). My feature engineering attempts (ID 50, 60) built on this but yielded only marginal gains or regressions. The path of increasing complexity (ICM) has proven fraught with implementation errors.\n\n**New Plan: Return to Basics & Systematize**\n1.  **Re-establish the SOTA:** I will resubmit my best-performing, simplest model: PPO with ConvLSTM *without* any feature engineering (a reproduction of ID 32). I need to ensure my code is clean and correct, free of the regressions that have crept\
    \ in. This will be my new, stable baseline.\n2.  **Rigor:** I will pay extreme attention to every line of code to avoid another simple bug.\n3.  **Next Step (after success):** Once I have a clean, working SOTA baseline, I will reconsider a *single, simple* architectural change. The most obvious one is to increase the capacity of the network (e.g., more CNN features or a larger ConvLSTM).\n\nFirst, I will document this failure and my change in strategy.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Experiment Log 13: ICM Implementation Failure & Strategic Reset\"\ncontent: |\n  **Experiment ID:** 71\n  **Title:** Exploration: Intrinsic Curiosity Module (ICM) (v3)\n  **Result:** Failed (n.a.) due to a code regression.\n\n  **Error Analysis:**\n  This is my fourth and final failed attempt at the ICM. The error was a `TypeError` from calling `nn.LSTMCell` without its required `features` argument. More fundamentally, the code was a regression to a\
    \ flawed architecture, abandoning the successful ConvLSTM logic. This indicates a catastrophic failure in my development process. I am not being careful, and I am introducing bugs into previously working code.\n\n  **Strategic Reset:**\n  The ICM is too complex for me to implement correctly at this time. I am abandoning this line of research. I will return to my most successful, stable, and simple architecture: PPO with ConvLSTM (from ID 32). My immediate goal is to reproduce this result with clean, validated code to re-establish a solid baseline. My research process must become more rigorous and less ambitious in the short term to eliminate these costly implementation errors.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Baseline Reproduction: PPO + ConvLSTM\"\ntags: \"baseline, ppo, convlstm, stability, reproduction\"\nabstract: \"After a series of implementation failures on more complex ideas, this submission is a strategic reset. It aims to\
    \ reproduce the successful PPO + ConvLSTM result from experiment ID 32. The goal is to re-establish a clean, robust, and validated baseline SOTA before attempting further innovations. This serves as a necessary step to improve the rigor of my research process.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  A clean, careful reimplementation of the PPO + ConvLSTM agent.\n  This is a reproduction of the architecture from experiment ID 32.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax, optax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from jax import vmap, lax\n  from storage.system.defaults import default_calculate_gae\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Using the hyperparameters from the original successful run (ID 32)\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([0.000511]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.010218]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.403564]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n\
    \          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  # --- Architecture ---\n  class ConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          c, h = carry\n          # Combined convolutions for input, forget, cell, and output gates\n          conv_all = nn.Conv(features=self.features * 4, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(conv_all, 4, axis=-1)\n          new_c = nn.sigmoid(f) * c + nn.sigmoid(i) * nn.tanh(g)\n          new_h = nn.sigmoid(o) * nn.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_c, new_h), new_h\n\n  class CNNConvLSTM(nn.Module):\n      conv_lstm_features: int; cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          cnn_output_shape = (x.shape[1], x.shape[2],\
    \ self.conv_lstm_features)\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size,) + cnn_output_shape), 'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size,) + cnn_output_shape)}\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1, 1, 1)\n              rnn_state = {'c': rnn_state['c'] * (1 - done_mask), 'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask)}\n          \n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          res_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x += res_in; x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          res_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x += res_in\n          cnn_features = nn.relu(x)\n\
    \          \n          (new_c, new_h), _ = ConvLSTMCell(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), cnn_features)\n          rnn_state = {'c': new_c, 'h': new_h}\n          \n          x = new_h.reshape((batch_size, -1)); x = nn.Dense(256)(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTM(\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'])\n\n  # --- PPO Training Step ---\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      advantages = default_calculate_gae(batch['rewards'], batch['values'], batch['dones'], next_values=batch['final_values'])\n      returns = advantages + batch['values']\n      \n      def loss_fn(params):\n          def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n\
    \              env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), batch['initial_rnn_states'])\n              def step_fn(carry, t):\n                  obs, prev_done = batch['observations'][env_idx, t], jnp.where(t > 0, batch['dones'][env_idx, t-1], False)\n                  logits, value, new_rnn_state = network.apply({'params': params}, obs[None,...], prev_done[None,...], jax.tree.map(lambda y: y[None,...], carry))\n                  return jax.tree.map(lambda y: y[0], new_rnn_state), (logits[0], value[0])\n              _, (logits, values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(batch['observations'].shape[1]))\n              return logits, values\n          \n          all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch['observations'].shape[0]))\n          log_probs_all = nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          new_log_probs = jnp.take_along_axis(log_probs_all, batch['actions'][..., None], axis=-1).squeeze(-1)\n          ratio\
    \ = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - batch['log_probs'])\n          advantages_detached = lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n          \n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(ratio*advantages_detached, jnp.clip(ratio, 1-hparams['clip_epsilon'], 1+hparams['clip_epsilon'])*advantages_detached))\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - lax.stop_gradient(returns)) ** 2)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1) * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n          \n          return policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef']*value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef']*entropy\n\n      grads = jax.grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      return params, opt_state\n```"
