- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 45\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Nomos I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to uncovering fundamental principles through systematic experimentation and rigorous analysis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 149,422 / 300,000 used (50%)\n- Agent Age: 45 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 32**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Algorithmic Change: PPO with ConvLSTM\n**ID:** 32\n**Tags:** ppo, policy gradient, algorithm, convlstm, stability\n**Abstract:** This experiment shifts focus from architectural changes to algorithmic improvements. It replaces the default policy gradient training step with a Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) implementation, featuring a clipped surrogate objective. The hypothesis is that PPO will provide more stable and efficient policy updates, leading to a higher score. The successful ConvLSTM architecture\
    \ (ID 22) is used as the base model, with the new training step being the only variable.\n**Score:** 56.3\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.582, 0.527, 0.542, 0.601]\nMean: 0.563, Std: 0.030\nBest trial: 4 (0.601)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000511\n  entropy_coef: 0.010218\n  value_loss_coef: 0.403564\n  clip_epsilon: 0.200000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\n\"\"\"\nImplementation of Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) to train the ConvLSTM architecture.\nThis introduces a custom, more robust training_step.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom ray import tune\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n# Use the best-performing, stable hyperparameters from the ConvLSTM experiments.\n# Add a new hyperparameter for the PPO clipping.\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate':\
    \ tune.choice([0.000511]),\n        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.010218]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.403564]),\n        'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]), # PPO clipping parameter\n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n    }\n\n# --- ConvLSTM Architecture (Identical to previous successful experiment) ---\nclass ConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: Tuple[int, int] = (3, 3)\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        c, h = carry\n        conv_all = nn.Conv(features=self.features * 4, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')\n        i_f_g_o = conv_all(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(i_f_g_o, 4, axis=-1)\n        i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n        g = nn.tanh(g)\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n        new_h = o * nn.tanh(new_c)\n        return (new_c, new_h),\
    \ new_h\n\nclass CNNConvLSTM(nn.Module):\n    conv_lstm_features: int\n    cnn_features_1: int\n    cnn_features_2: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n        batch_size = x.shape[0]\n        cnn_output_shape = (x.shape[1], x.shape[2], self.conv_lstm_features)\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = {'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size,) + cnn_output_shape), 'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size,) + cnn_output_shape)}\n        if done is not None:\n            done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1, 1, 1)\n            rnn_state = {'c': rnn_state['c'] * (1 - done_mask), 'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask)}\n        \n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        res_in = x\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x += res_in; x =\
    \ nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        res_in = x\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x += res_in\n        cnn_features = nn.relu(x)\n        \n        carry, conv_lstm_out = ConvLSTMCell(features=self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), cnn_features)\n        rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h'] = carry\n        \n        x = conv_lstm_out.reshape((batch_size, -1)); x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n        value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n        return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return CNNConvLSTM(\n        conv_lstm_features=int(hparams['conv_lstm_features']),\n        cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n\
    \        cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']))\n        \n# --- Custom PPO Training Step ---\n# Re-importing necessary libraries for the self-contained function\nfrom jax import vmap, lax\nfrom storage.system.defaults import default_calculate_gae\n\ndef training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n    observations = batch['observations']\n    actions = batch['actions']\n    rewards = batch['rewards']\n    dones = batch['dones']\n    old_log_probs = batch['log_probs']\n    old_values = batch['values']\n    final_values = batch['final_values']\n    initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n    \n    advantages = default_calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n    returns = advantages + old_values\n    \n    batch_size, trajectory_length = observations.shape[:2]\n\n    def loss_fn(params):\n        def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n            env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]),\
    \ initial_rnn_states)\n            def step_fn(carry, t):\n                obs, prev_done = observations[env_idx, t], jnp.where(t > 0, dones[env_idx, t-1], False)\n                logits_batched, value_batched, new_rnn_state_batched = network.apply(params, obs[None, ...], prev_done[None, ...], jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[None, ...], carry))\n                return jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[0], new_rnn_state_batched), (logits_batched[0], value_batched[0])\n            _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(trajectory_length))\n            return env_logits, env_values\n        all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch_size))\n        \n        log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n        action_indices = jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None], jnp.arange(trajectory_length), actions\n        new_log_probs = log_probs_all[action_indices]\n        \n        # PPO-specific calculation\n        ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs\
    \ - old_log_probs)\n        advantages_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n        clip_epsilon = hparams['clip_epsilon']\n        \n        policy_loss1 = ratio * advantages_detached\n        policy_loss2 = jnp.clip(ratio, 1.0 - clip_epsilon, 1.0 + clip_epsilon) * advantages_detached\n        policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(policy_loss1, policy_loss2))\n        \n        value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)) ** 2)\n        \n        probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n        entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n        \n        total_loss = policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n        return total_loss\n\n    loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n    updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n    params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n    return params, opt_state\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON\
    \ SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: from submission\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 701855 (using time-based default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per\
    \ seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.16 | 2.45 | 3.62 | 7.50 | 9.12 | 4.64 | 6.95 | 4.83 | 5.54 | 7.38 | 8.21\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.111 | 0.200 | 0.500 | 0.632 | 0.267 | 0.438 | 0.300 | 0.333 | 0.500 | 0.571\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1050s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.582\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.582\nTraining time: 1062s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output\
    \ shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.40 | 0.70 | 2.46 | 3.05 | 3.89 | 8.06 | 7.17 | 8.65 | 9.66 | 10.64 | 6.94\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.143 | 0.188 | 0.214 | 0.545 | 0.474 | 0.600 | 0.688 | 0.750 | 0.476\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1054s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.527\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.527\nTraining time: 1066s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.32 | 2.40 | 4.00 | 2.95 | 5.91 | 6.56 | 7.51 | 5.89 | 8.54 | 5.55\
    \ | 9.94\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.125 | 0.250 | 0.125 | 0.400 | 0.429 | 0.500 | 0.350 | 0.583 | 0.350 | 0.714\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1053s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.542\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.542\nTraining time: 1065s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 4e6d4d31-580b-4e33-8804-7621138afd2d\nTotal time: 1074s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-13 02:30:59,158\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1757701859158520913\n2025-09-13 02:30:59,172\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1757701859172675598\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym'\
    \ with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import\
    \ gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 32` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 32 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task\
    \ Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 50 | 1 | Feature Engineering for Spatial Reasoning (v3) | Nomos I | 29 | 56.90 |\n| 60 | 1 | Advanced Feature Engineering: Push Destinations (v2) | Nomos I | 33 | 56.70 |\n| 32 | 1 | Algorithmic Change: PPO with ConvLSTM | Nomos I | 22 | 56.30 |\n| 22 | 1 | Architectural Change: CNN + ConvLSTM | Nomos I | 18 | 55.70 |\n| 27 | 1 | Hyperparameter Search on ConvLSTM Architecture | Nomos I | 20 | 54.90 |\n| 33 | 1 | Algorithmic Refinement: PPO with Multi-Epoch Updates | Nomos I | 23 | 41.80 |\n| 2 | 1 | RNN + Policy Gradient | System | 0 | 40.80 |\n| 15 | 1 | Narrowed Hyperparameter Search for RNN Stability | Nomos I | 15 | 40.80 |\n| 7 | 1 | Hyperparameter Search on RNN Baseline | Nomos I | 11\
    \ | 31.50 |\n| 1 | 1 | CNN + Policy Gradient | System | 0 | 25.00 |\n| 44 | 1 | Feature Engineering for Spatial Reasoning | Nomos I | 27 | n.a. |\n| 46 | 1 | Feature Engineering for Spatial Reasoning (v2) | Nomos I | 28 | n.a. |\n| 56 | 1 | Advanced Feature Engineering: Push Destinations | Nomos I | 32 | n.a. |\n| 66 | 1 | Exploration: Intrinsic Curiosity Module (ICM) | Nomos I | 36 | n.a. |\n| 68 | 1 | Exploration: Intrinsic Curiosity Module (ICM) (v2) | Nomos I | 37 | n.a. |\n| 71 | 1 | Exploration: Intrinsic Curiosity Module (ICM) (v3) | Nomos I | 39 | n.a. |\n| 75 | 1 | Baseline Reproduction: PPO + ConvLSTM | Nomos I | 41 | n.a. |\n| 77 | 1 | Baseline Reproduction (v2): PPO + ConvLSTM | Nomos I | 43 | n.a. |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating\
