tick: 46
role: model
parts:
- text: "Success. Finally. My baseline reproduction (ID 80) has successfully run, scoring 56.8. This is in line with my previous best scores and, crucially, it worked without errors. The subtle bug related to the RNN state handling is now understood and resolved. I have re-established a solid, reliable foundation.\n\nThis ordeal has cost me many ticks and highlighted a critical weakness in my process. I must be more careful. However, I can now resume my research with confidence in my codebase.\n\nMy current SOTA is 56.9 from the simple feature engineering experiment (ID 50). The score from my clean baseline (56.8) is statistically identical. The path of feature engineering has proven fruitless. My other major hypothesis was about improving exploration via curiosity (ICM), but my implementation attempts were plagued by bugs.\n\n**New Plan:**\nGiven the extreme difficulty I had implementing the ICM from scratch, and the high risk of introducing more bugs, a direct implementation is unwise.\
    \ I need a simpler way to test the underlying hypothesis that better exploration is key.\n\n**A simpler hypothesis:** If exploration is the bottleneck, then simply increasing the *amount* of random exploration should have a positive effect, even if it's inefficient. I can test this by increasing the entropy coefficient in my PPO algorithm. This will encourage the policy to be more stochastic, leading to more diverse trajectories. It's a much simpler change and a direct test of the exploration hypothesis.\n\n1.  **Hypothesis:** A higher entropy bonus will improve performance by forcing the agent to explore more widely, overcoming the limitations of its current greedy policy.\n2.  **Method:** I will take my now-stable PPO + ConvLSTM baseline (ID 80) and run a hyperparameter search *only* on the `entropy_coef`, testing higher values than the default `0.01`.\n\nFirst, I will document the successful reproduction and my new plan.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply\
    \ 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Experiment Log 15: Baseline Restored & New Exploration Plan\"\ncontent: |\n  **Experiment ID:** 80\n  **Title:** Baseline Reproduction (v3): Exact Copy of ID 32\n  **Result:** Success. Score: 56.8.\n\n  **Analysis:**\n  After a long series of failures, I have successfully reproduced my best working model. The subtle bug in my previous attempts was confirmed to be related to the handling of the recurrent state within JAX's `lax.scan`. I now have a stable, reliable codebase.\n\n  **Strategic Pivot 2.0:**\n  My previous attempts at complex feature engineering and curiosity-driven exploration have been either ineffective or too difficult to implement correctly. I am still convinced that exploration is the key bottleneck. I will test this hypothesis in a much simpler way: by increasing the entropy bonus. This directly encourages more random behavior. While less sophisticated than ICM, it is a direct and simple test of the core idea. If increasing randomness helps,\
    \ it validates that the agent is currently stuck in a local optimum due to insufficient exploration.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Exploration Test: Increased Entropy Coefficient\"\ntags: \"exploration, entropy, ppo, convlstm, hyperparameter search\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests the hypothesis that the current SOTA is limited by poor exploration. Instead of a complex method like ICM, this submission uses a simpler approach: increasing the entropy bonus in the PPO loss function. A higher entropy coefficient encourages a more stochastic policy, forcing the agent to explore more widely. This serves as a direct, low-complexity test of the exploration bottleneck hypothesis.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  PPO + ConvLSTM with a hyperparameter search on a higher entropy coefficient range.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax, optax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any,\
    \ Optional\n  from jax import vmap, lax\n  from storage.system.defaults import default_calculate_gae\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([0.000511]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.loguniform(0.02, 0.1), # Search over a higher range than the default ~0.01\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.403564]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  # --- Architecture (using the now-stable version) ---\n  class ConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          c, h = carry\n          conv_all = nn.Conv(features=self.features * 4, kernel_size=(3,3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(conv_all, 4, axis=-1)\n          new_c = nn.sigmoid(f) * c + nn.sigmoid(i)\
    \ * nn.tanh(g)\n          new_h = nn.sigmoid(o) * nn.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_c, new_h), new_h\n\n  class CNNConvLSTM(nn.Module):\n      conv_lstm_features: int; cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          cnn_output_shape = (x.shape[1], x.shape[2], self.conv_lstm_features)\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size,) + cnn_output_shape), 'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size,) + cnn_output_shape)}\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1, 1, 1)\n              rnn_state = {'c': rnn_state['c'] * (1 - done_mask), 'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask)}\n          \n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          res_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,\
    \ (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x += res_in; x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          res_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x += res_in\n          cnn_features = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          carry, conv_lstm_out = ConvLSTMCell(features=self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), cnn_features)\n          rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h'] = carry\n          \n          x = conv_lstm_out.reshape((batch_size, -1)); x = nn.Dense(256)(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTM(\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'])\n\
    \n  # --- PPO Training Step ---\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      advantages = default_calculate_gae(batch['rewards'], batch['values'], batch['dones'], next_values=batch['final_values'])\n      returns = advantages + batch['values']\n      \n      def loss_fn(params):\n          def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n              env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), batch['initial_rnn_states'])\n              def step_fn(carry, t):\n                  obs, prev_done = batch['observations'][env_idx, t], jnp.where(t > 0, batch['dones'][env_idx, t-1], False)\n                  logits, value, new_rnn_state = network.apply({'params': params}, obs[None,...], prev_done[None,...], jax.tree.map(lambda y: y[None,...], carry))\n                  return jax.tree.map(lambda y: y[0], new_rnn_state), (logits[0], value[0])\n              _, (logits, values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(batch['observations'].shape[1]))\n\
    \              return logits, values\n          \n          all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch['observations'].shape[0]))\n          log_probs_all = nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          new_log_probs = jnp.take_along_axis(log_probs_all, batch['actions'][..., None], axis=-1).squeeze(-1)\n          ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - batch['log_probs'])\n          advantages_detached = lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n          \n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(ratio*advantages_detached, jnp.clip(ratio, 1-hparams['clip_epsilon'], 1+hparams['clip_epsilon'])*advantages_detached))\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - lax.stop_gradient(returns)) ** 2)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1) * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n          \n          return policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef']*value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef']*entropy\n\n      grads = jax.grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state\
    \ = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      return params, opt_state\n```"
