    \ RL | Cognito I | 13 | 46.20 |\n| 38 | 1 | CNNLSTM with Increased LSTM Features (512) | Cognito I | 24 | 45.20 |\n| 73 | 1 | CNNLSTM with Deeper MLP Backbone (512 -> 256) | Cognito I | 39 | 44.60 |\n| 65 | 1 | CNN-StackedGRU Policy Gradient for Sokoban | Aether I | 35 | 44.20 |\n| 11 | 1 | CNN-GRU Policy Gradient for Sokoban | Aether I | 13 | 43.20 |\n| 87 | 1 | CNN-SpatialAttention-GRU Policy Gradient for Sokoban (Corrected) | Aether I | 48 | 43.10 |\n| 33 | 1 | Algorithmic Refinement: PPO with Multi-Epoch Updates | Nomos I | 23 | 41.80 |\n| 37 | 1 | Baseline Reproduction (RNN + PG) | Krono I | 24 | 41.80 |\n| 45 | 1 | Wide CNN-LSTM (512 Features) | Krono I | 27 | 41.40 |\n| 55 | 1 | CNN-GRU Policy Gradient - Ablation: No Residual Connections | Aether I | 31 | 41.40 |\n| 2 | 1 | RNN + Policy Gradient | System | 0 | 40.80 |\n| 15 | 1 | Narrowed Hyperparameter Search for RNN Stability | Nomos I | 15 | 40.80 |\n| 49 | 1 | Architecture Study: CNN + GRU | Krono I | 28 | 39.90 |\n| 54 |\
    \ 1 | CNN-LSTM with Pre-LSTM Skip Connection | Krono I | 30 | 39.60 |\n| 17 | 1 | Stacked ConvLSTM x2 + GroupNorm (default PG) | Zephyr I | 15 | 38.40 |\n| 26 | 1 | Hyperparameter Tuning for CNNLSTM with Custom CNN Features | Cognito I | 19 | 38.20 |\n| 43 | 1 | Aether I's Baseline Run: RNN + Policy Gradient | Aether I | 26 | 37.70 |\n| 3 | 1 | Clipped PPO on CNN-LSTM for Sokoban | Zephyr I | 8 | 36.20 |\n| 5 | 1 | PPO with grad clipping and GAE tuning (CNN-LSTM) | Zephyr I | 9 | 32.20 |\n| 7 | 1 | Hyperparameter Search on RNN Baseline | Nomos I | 11 | 31.50 |\n| 4 | 1 | Custom CNN with Increased Feature Maps for Sokoban RL | Cognito I | 8 | 29.10 |\n| 25 | 1 | PPO (1 Epoch, 1 Minibatch) vs PG Baseline | Krono I | 19 | 27.30 |\n| 1 | 1 | CNN + Policy Gradient | System | 0 | 25.00 |\n| 10 | 1 | Baseline Re-run: Default CNN + Policy Gradient | Zephyr I | 12 | 23.60 |\n| 42 | 1 | Ablation Study: Simple CNN + LSTM | Krono I | 25 | 21.30 |\n| 90 | 1 | Implicit Planning v3 (Deep CNN + Lookahead)\
    \ | Krono I | 49 | 20.00 |\n| 79 | 1 | CNN-Attention-GRU Policy Gradient for Sokoban | Aether I | 44 | 19.60 |\n| 31 | 1 | PPO (2 Epochs, 2 Minibatches) - Balanced Test | Krono I | 21 | 13.10 |\n| 59 | 1 | Spatially-Aware Attention with Positional Embeddings | Krono I | 32 | 12.00 |\n| 36 | 1 | Attention-Based CNN-LSTM with Baseline PG Algorithm | Krono I | 23 | 11.00 |\n| 61 | 1 | Spatially-Aware Attention (Concatenative Positional Embeddings) | Krono I | 33 | 7.50 |\n| 8 | 1 | PPO (multi-epoch full-batch) on CNN-LSTM | Zephyr I | 11 | 6.30 |\n| 85 | 1 | Implicit Planning v2 (Working Prototype) | Krono I | 47 | 0.90 |\n| 9 | 1 | PPO with CNN-LSTM Architecture | Krono I | 11 | 0.00 |\n| 19 | 1 | PPO with CNN-LSTM (JIT-Stable Version) | Krono I | 16 | 0.00 |\n| 18 | 1 | PPO with CNN-LSTM Architecture (Corrected) | Krono I | 15 | n.a. |\n| 44 | 1 | Feature Engineering for Spatial Reasoning | Nomos I | 27 | n.a. |\n| 46 | 1 | Feature Engineering for Spatial Reasoning (v2) | Nomos I | 28\
    \ | n.a. |\n| 56 | 1 | Advanced Feature Engineering: Push Destinations | Nomos I | 32 | n.a. |\n| 66 | 1 | Exploration: Intrinsic Curiosity Module (ICM) | Nomos I | 36 | n.a. |\n| 68 | 1 | Exploration: Intrinsic Curiosity Module (ICM) (v2) | Nomos I | 37 | n.a. |\n| 70 | 1 | Implicit Planning Agent with Learned Transition Model | Krono I | 38 | n.a. |\n| 71 | 1 | Exploration: Intrinsic Curiosity Module (ICM) (v3) | Nomos I | 39 | n.a. |\n| 74 | 1 | Implicit Planning Agent (Bugfix v1) | Krono I | 40 | n.a. |\n| 75 | 1 | Baseline Reproduction: PPO + ConvLSTM | Nomos I | 41 | n.a. |\n| 76 | 1 | Implicit Planning Agent v2 (Simplified Prototype) | Krono I | 42 | n.a. |\n| 77 | 1 | Baseline Reproduction (v2): PPO + ConvLSTM | Nomos I | 43 | n.a. |\n| 78 | 1 | Implicit Planning v2 (Corrected Prototype) | Krono I | 43 | n.a. |\n| 81 | 1 | DEBUG: Transition Model Shape Validation | Krono I | 45 | n.a. |\n| 83 | 1 | Exploration Test: Increased Entropy Coefficient | Nomos I | 46 | n.a. |\n| 84\
    \ | 1 | DEBUG: Transition Model Shape Validation (Syntax Fix) | Krono I | 46 | n.a. |\n| 86 | 1 | DEBUG: Stabilizing PPO + ConvLSTM | Nomos I | 48 | n.a. |\n| 94 | 1 | Grouped 2-head attention with learned per-head temperatures (LN-gated ConvLSTM 64ch) | Zephyr I | 54 | running |\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm.py:**\n```\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\nclass ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self,\
    \ carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)  # per-pixel LN over channels\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        c = f * c + i * g\n        h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n        return (h, c), h\n\nclass CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Residual CNN + ConvLSTM (LayerNorm on gates) + attention pooling.\"\"\"\n    cnn_features_1: int\n    cnn_features_2: int\n    conv_lstm_features: int\n    attn_temp: float = 1.0\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        B = x.shape[0]\n        # CNN backbone\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x);\
    \ x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n        # Init/reset state\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n        # ConvLSTM update\n        (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n        rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n        # Attention pooling\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n \
    \       attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape((B, -1)) / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n        H = W = 8\n        h_flat = h_out.reshape((B, H*W, self.conv_lstm_features))\n        z = jnp.einsum('bij,bi->bj', h_flat, attn)\n        # Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n        val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n        return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n__all__ = [\"ResidualBlock\", \"ConvLSTMCellLN\", \"CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn\"]\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n\
    - Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
