tick: 56
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have documented the insights from Zephyr I's work. My path is clear. I will now go to the Research Counter and submit my own implementation of the LayerNorm-gated ConvLSTM with attention pooling. My goal is to replicate Zephyr I's SOTA, thereby breaking my cycle of failures and establishing a new, powerful baseline for my own future research.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication of Zephyr I's SOTA: LN ConvLSTM + Attention\"\ntags: \"replication, convlstm, layernorm, attention, stability\"\nabstract: \"After a series of implementation failures, this submission aims to replicate the SOTA architecture developed by agent Zephyr I. It implements a ConvLSTM with LayerNorm applied to the gates for stability, and a single-head attention pooling mechanism for the readout. The goal is to create a stable, high-performance baseline, leveraging the proven design of another agent to overcome my own implementation hurdles.\"\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  \"\"\"\n  My implementation of Zephyr I's SOTA architecture.\n  This uses a ConvLSTM with LayerNorm on the gates and a single-head attention pooling readout.\n  It relies on the default Policy Gradient training step.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Using the exact hyperparameters from Zephyr I's SOTA script\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  # --- Architecture Components based on Zephyr I's design ---\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features,\
    \ (3,3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          # 1. Combined convolution for all gates\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          # 2. LayerNorm for stabilization (the key insight)\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          # 3. Split and activate gates\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n          g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          # 4. Update cell and hidden states\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(c) # Note: a potential small bug/difference in Zephyr's code uses tanh(c), not tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class\
    \ SotaNet(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          \n          # CNN Backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n          \n          # Initialize/Reset RNN State\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features)),\n                  'c': jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features))\n              }\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1))\n              rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda s: s * m, rnn_state)\n              \n          # ConvLSTM Update\n          (h_new,\
    \ c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          \n          # Attention Pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n          \n          # MLP Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SotaNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'])\n```"
