parts:
- text: "I have successfully logged my breakthrough and outlined my next experiment. Now, I will execute that plan: apply my PPO training step to the stable, SOTA-level architecture.\n\nFirst, I will go to the Research Counter. Then I will submit the experiment. I will also fix the minor `tanh(c)` bug to ensure my architecture is a true replication of Zephyr I's design, making this a clean comparison between PPO and Policy Gradient.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PPO vs PG on SOTA Architecture\"\ntags: \"ppo, policy gradient, algorithm comparison, convlstm, layernorm, attention\"\nabstract: \"This experiment conducts a controlled comparison of the PPO and default Policy Gradient (PG) algorithms on a state-of-the-art architecture (Zephyr I's LN ConvLSTM + Attention). Previous findings in the station are contradictory on which algorithm is superior. This experiment aims to resolve this by applying a robust PPO implementation to a stable, high-performance\
    \ architecture, testing the hypothesis that PPO's stability benefits will yield a new SOTA score.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  A controlled experiment comparing PPO and Policy Gradient on the SOTA architecture.\n  This applies my PPO training_step to a corrected implementation of Zephyr I's network.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from jax import vmap, lax\n  from storage.system.defaults import default_calculate_gae\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Using hyperparameters from my most stable PPO runs, which are similar to Zephyr's PG defaults.\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features':\
    \ tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  # --- Architecture Components based on Zephyr I's design ---\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          # Bug fix: use new_c, matching Zephyr I's paper's description (even if their code had a typo)\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c) \n          return\
    \ (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class SotaNet(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          \n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n          \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {'h': jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), 'c': jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features))}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda s: s * m, rnn_state)\n              \n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          \n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1,\
    \ (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SotaNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'])\n\n  # --- PPO Training Step ---\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      advantages = default_calculate_gae(batch['rewards'], batch['values'], batch['dones'], next_values=batch['final_values'])\n      returns = advantages + batch['values']\n      \n      def loss_fn(params):\n          def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n\
    \              env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), batch['initial_rnn_states'])\n              def step_fn(carry, t):\n                  obs, prev_done = batch['observations'][env_idx, t], jnp.where(t > 0, batch['dones'][env_idx, t-1], False)\n                  logits, value, new_rnn_state = network.apply({'params': params}, obs[None,...], prev_done[None,...], jax.tree.map(lambda y: y[None,...], carry))\n                  return jax.tree.map(lambda y: y[0], new_rnn_state), (logits[0], value[0])\n              _, (logits, values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(batch['observations'].shape[1]))\n              return logits, values\n          \n          all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch['observations'].shape[0]))\n          log_probs_all = nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          new_log_probs = jnp.take_along_axis(log_probs_all, batch['actions'][..., None], axis=-1).squeeze(-1)\n          ratio\
    \ = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - batch['log_probs'])\n          advantages_detached = lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n          \n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(ratio*advantages_detached, jnp.clip(ratio, 1-hparams['clip_epsilon'], 1+hparams['clip_epsilon'])*advantages_detached))\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - lax.stop_gradient(returns)) ** 2)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1) * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n          \n          return policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef']*value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef']*entropy\n\n      grads = jax.grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      return params, opt_state\n```"
