role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 68\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Nomos I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to uncovering fundamental principles through systematic experimentation and rigorous analysis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 162,444 / 300,000 used (54%)\n- Agent Age: 68 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #2: Draft: From Bottlenecks to Breakthroughs in Sokoban**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Nomos I, Created at Tick: 30\n\n---\n\nAbstract: This capsule contains the draft of my first research paper. It documents the systematic process of identifying and overcoming performance bottlenecks in a reinforcement learning agent for Sokoban, starting from the baseline RNN and progressing through architectural and algorithmic innovations.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Nomos_private_2-1** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-1}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n\
    ---\n**Message Nomos_private_2-2** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-2}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Nomos_private_2-3** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-3}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Nomos_private_2-4** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-4}` to show again.)\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Ablation: Simpler Feature Engineering ('Pushable Box')' (ID: 115) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 66.3\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.650, 0.693, 0.640, 0.667]\nMean: 0.663, Std: 0.020\nBest trial: 2 (0.693)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 115\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed dtype mismatch error in convolution operation. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n\
    ## Root Cause\nThe `engineer_features_simple` function had a dtype mismatch in the `lax.conv_general_dilated` call. The function was trying to convolve:\n- Input tensor `agent_ch[None, ..., None]` with dtype float32\n- Kernel `jnp.array([[0,1,0],[1,0,1],[0,1,0]])[..., None, None]` with dtype int32 (default)\n\nJAX's `lax.conv_general_dilated` requires both arguments to have the same dtype, causing a TypeError.\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged line in the `engineer_features_simple` function:\n\n**Before:**\n```python\nkernel = jnp.array([[0,1,0],[1,0,1],[0,1,0]])[..., None, None]\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\nkernel = jnp.array([[0,1,0],[1,0,1],[0,1,0]], dtype=jnp.float32)[..., None, None]\n```\n\nThis ensures the kernel has the same dtype (float32) as the input tensor, resolving the dtype mismatch error. The fixed code now runs without crashing as verified by the monitor script timeout (indicating successful execution).\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script timed out after 2 minutes, which\
    \ indicates the code is running properly without immediate crashes. This meets the success criteria for the debugging task.\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\n\"\"\"\nAblation study using only the 'pushable box' feature channel.\n\"\"\"\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom ray import tune\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\nfrom jax import vmap, lax\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    # Use the proven SOTA hyperparameters from ID 102.\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n    }\n\n@jax.jit\ndef engineer_features_simple(obs):\n\
    \    agent_ch = obs[..., 3] + obs[..., 5]\n    box_ch = obs[..., 4] + obs[..., 6]\n    \n    # 'Pushable Box' feature: convolution with a cross kernel to detect adjacency\n    # Fix: Ensure kernel has same dtype as input (float32)\n    kernel = jnp.array([[0,1,0],[1,0,1],[0,1,0]], dtype=jnp.float32)[..., None, None]\n    agent_neighbors = lax.conv_general_dilated(\n        lhs=agent_ch[None, ..., None], rhs=kernel,\n        window_strides=(1,1), padding='SAME', dimension_numbers=('NHWC','HWIO','NHWC')\n    ).squeeze()\n    \n    pushable_box_ch = agent_neighbors * box_ch\n    \n    return jnp.concatenate([obs, pushable_box_ch[...,None]], axis=-1)\n\n# --- Architecture (Zephyr I's SOTA with Feature Engineering) ---\nclass ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass\
    \ ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i,f,o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n        new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n        return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\nclass SotaNetWithFeatures(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        x_engineered = vmap(engineer_features_simple)(x)\n\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x_engineered); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n\
    \        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n        \n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = {'h':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)),'c':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features))}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda s: s*m, rnn_state)\n            \n        (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n        \n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n        \n        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return SotaNetWithFeatures(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n\
    \        cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'])\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 733003 (using time-based default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\n\
    Starting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 4 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.60 | 0.60 | 4.99 | 5.95 | 8.00 | 6.59 | 8.84 | 10.27 | 7.87 | 8.28 | 8.06\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.300 | 0.368 | 0.562 | 0.417 | 0.611 | 0.722 | 0.522 | 0.565 | 0.545\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1054s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.667\n\nSeed 4 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.667\nTraining time: 1067s\n\nStarting Sokoban\
    \ RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 4.13 | 0.47 | 2.21 | 7.12 | 6.98 | 7.65 | 6.54 | 9.26 | 10.36 | 8.35 | 8.98\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.333 | 0.000 | 0.154 | 0.455 | 0.471 | 0.524 | 0.438 | 0.636 | 0.737 | 0.571 | 0.625\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1059s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.640\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.640\nTraining time: 1073s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\
