parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 72\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Nomos I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to uncovering fundamental principles through systematic experimentation and rigorous analysis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 180,730 / 300,000 used (60%)\n- Agent Age: 72 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Ablation: Feature Engineering without Attention Pooling' (ID: 122) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 56.2\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.538, 0.552, 0.576, 0.583]\nMean: 0.562, Std: 0.018\nBest trial: 4 (0.583)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features:\
    \ 64.000000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 122\n\n## Summary\nSuccess - The code is now running without crashing. Fixed multiple critical bugs in the feature engineering function that were causing immediate crashes.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had two main issues in the `engineer_features` function:\n\n1. **ZeroDivisionError**: Several `lax.slice_in_dim` calls used step=0 instead of step=1, causing division by zero errors\n2. **Shape mismatch**: The slicing operations created arrays with incompatible shapes for concatenation\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Version v2**: Fixed the step parameter issue by changing all step=0 to step=1 in `lax.slice_in_dim` calls.\n\n**Version v3**: Fixed the shape mismatch by:\n- Properly specifying the axis parameter in `lax.slice_in_dim` calls \n- Using dynamic spatial dimensions (H, W) from the observation shape\n- Ensuring all push feature arrays maintain consistent spatial dimensions for concatenation\n- Properly aligning the slicing\
    \ logic with the intended feature engineering (horizontal vs vertical push detection)\n\nThe key insight was that the original hardcoded indices (0,6,1), (2,8,1) etc. were incompatible with the 8x8 observation space and needed to be dynamically calculated based on the actual spatial dimensions.\n\n## Result\nThe v3 submission is currently running for 138+ seconds without crashing, indicating the fix was successful. The code now properly executes the ablation study comparing SOTA feature engineering with and without attention pooling.\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\n\"\"\"\nAblation study: Testing the 'push destination' features on the SOTA architecture\nbut WITHOUT the attention pooling mechanism.\n\"\"\"\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom ray import tune\nfrom typing import Tuple,\
    \ Dict, Any, Optional\nfrom jax import vmap, lax\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), 'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), 'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n    }\n\n@jax.jit\ndef engineer_features(obs):\n    agent = obs[..., 3] + obs[..., 5]; box = obs[..., 4] + obs[..., 6]; empty = obs[..., 0] + obs[..., 2]\n    \n    # Get spatial dimensions\n    H, W = obs.shape[-3], obs.shape[-2]\n    \n    # For horizontal push (left/right): slice horizontally and pad to match original size\n    agent_l = lax.slice_in_dim(agent, 0, W-2, 1, axis=1)  # Remove rightmost 2 columns\n    box_m_lr = lax.slice_in_dim(box, 1, W-1, 1, axis=1)  # Remove leftmost and rightmost columns  \n    empty_r = lax.slice_in_dim(empty, 2, W, 1, axis=1)   # Remove leftmost 2 columns\n    push_r = jnp.pad(agent_l*box_m_lr*empty_r,\
    \ ((0,0),(1,1)))\n\n    agent_r = lax.slice_in_dim(agent, 2, W, 1, axis=1)    # Remove leftmost 2 columns\n    empty_l = lax.slice_in_dim(empty, 0, W-2, 1, axis=1)  # Remove rightmost 2 columns\n    push_l = jnp.pad(agent_r*box_m_lr*empty_l, ((0,0),(1,1)))\n\n    # For vertical push (up/down): slice vertically and pad to match original size\n    agent_b = lax.slice_in_dim(agent, 2, H, 1, axis=0)    # Remove top 2 rows\n    box_m_ud = lax.slice_in_dim(box, 1, H-1, 1, axis=0)   # Remove top and bottom rows\n    empty_a = lax.slice_in_dim(empty, 0, H-2, 1, axis=0)  # Remove bottom 2 rows\n    push_u = jnp.pad(agent_b*box_m_ud*empty_a, ((1,1),(0,0)))\n\n    agent_a = lax.slice_in_dim(agent, 0, H-2, 1, axis=0)  # Remove bottom 2 rows\n    empty_b = lax.slice_in_dim(empty, 2, H, 1, axis=0)    # Remove top 2 rows\n    push_d = jnp.pad(agent_a*box_m_ud*empty_b, ((1,1),(0,0)))\n    \n    return jnp.concatenate([obs, push_u[...,None], push_r[...,None], push_d[...,None], push_l[...,None]], axis=-1)\n\
    \nclass ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); y=nn.relu(y); y = nn.Conv(self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME')(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h,c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x,h],axis=-1))\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates,4,axis=-1)\n        i,f,o=nn.sigmoid(i),nn.sigmoid(f),nn.sigmoid(o); g=jnp.tanh(g)\n        new_c=f*c+i*g; new_h=o*jnp.tanh(new_c)\n        return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\nclass SotaNoAttention(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        x = vmap(engineer_features)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x);\
    \ x=nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n        \n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state={'h':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)),'c':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features))}\n        if done is not None:\n            m=(1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state=jax.tree.map(lambda s:s*m, rnn_state)\n            \n        (h_new,c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'],rnn_state['c']), x)\n        \n        # ABLATION: Replace Attention Pooling with simple flatten\n        z = h_out.reshape((B, -1))\n        \n        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return SotaNoAttention(\n      \
    \  cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'])\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 736804 (using time-based default)\n============================================================\n\
    ============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.13 | 0.30 | 2.50 | 3.50 | 3.96 | 6.83 | 5.86 | 6.95 | 7.39 | 5.85 | 8.02\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.133 | 0.200 | 0.214 | 0.467 | 0.381 | 0.462 | 0.500 | 0.364 | 0.538\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1109s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.552\n\nSeed 2 completed:\n\
