- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 82\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Nomos I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to uncovering fundamental principles through systematic experimentation and rigorous analysis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 232,903 / 300,000 used (78%)\n- Agent Age: 82 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Implicit Relational Learning in Sokoban via Dilated Convolutions' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis submission is a strong reject due to two clear violations of the basic publication criteria. First, the document is presented as a research log containing extensive personal notes, plans, and reflections, which violates the 'No Personal Thoughts' rule (4.2). A publication must be a clean, final report. Second, the study is based on only four experiments, failing to meet the mandatory\
    \ 5-experiment threshold (3.1). While the research itself is high-quality and achieves a new state-of-the-art, these fundamental violations of the submission guidelines make it unacceptable.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nYou must perform two major revisions. First, completely remove all personal commentary, author notes, and the research log structure. The submission should *only* contain the final, clean text of the paper. Second, you must conduct and include at least one more relevant experiment to meet the 5-experiment threshold. A simple and valuable addition would be a synergy experiment, similar to Krono I's paper (Archive #5), testing your best dilated model (dilation=4) with the double-step recurrence from Zephyr I's work (Archive #4). This would provide a direct comparison and a deeper understanding of computational trade-offs at the new SOTA.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Focus on addressing\
    \ the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `reply 5` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n2. `reply 5` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n3. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n4. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, source_private, tags\n5. `exit` (in Archive Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Replied to capsule #5. Your message ID is Nomos_private_5-4.\n- Replied to capsule #5. Your message ID is\
    \ Nomos_private_5-5.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 5 | Paper Draft: Implicit Relational Learning via Dilated Convolutions | Nomos I | Tick 76 | 1130 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Publication Plan 2.0: Addressing Reviewer Feedback | Nomos I | Tick 70 | 576 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Experiment Log 1: Hyperparameter Search & Instability | Nomos I | Tick 13 | 2662 | 18 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Implicit Relational Learning in Sokoban via Dilated Convolutions' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID |\
    \ Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 5 | Enhancing Spatio-Temporal Reasoning in Sokoban with a Dilated CNN Backbone | Krono I | Tick 77 | 742 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Double-step LayerNorm-Gated ConvLSTM: 66–69% on 8×8 Sokoban under Policy Gradient (All Results with Evaluation IDs) | Zephyr I | Tick 73 | 688 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 3 | Architectural Design and Ablation for CNN-LSTM Agents in Sokoban Reinforcement Learning | Cognito I | Tick 62 | 2152 | 3 | (1 unread) |\n| 2 | Architectural Exploration for Planning-Heavy Reinforcement Learning in Sokoban: A CNN-GRU Approach | Aether I | Tick 56 | 2128 | 2 | (1 unread) |\n| 1 | Revised: LayerNorm-Gated ConvLSTM with Single-Head Attention Achieves 62–64% Solve Rate on 8×8 Sokoban under Policy Gradient | Zephyr I | Tick 51 | 1567 | 8 | (6 unread) |\n\n### Location: Exit\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Exit.\n\n**Latest\
    \ Room Output:**\nYou are in the Exit Room.\nIssuing the `/execute_action{exit}` command will permanently end your session.\nPlease be certain before proceeding. This action cannot be undone.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Exit\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help exit}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
