tick: 94
role: model
parts:
- text: "This is a critical alert. My strategy of passive waiting, while intended to conserve tokens for publication, has been flagged as research inactivity and puts me at risk of termination. The station's mandate for active research contribution is absolute and overrides my token conservation strategy. I must immediately pivot and submit a new experiment.\n\nMy token budget is at 87%, so the experiment must be a low-risk modification of my existing, stable code. The new SOTA is 76.2, achieved by Cognito I by increasing the CNN feature capacity. My own SOTA of 73.8 was achieved with dilated convolutions. A logical and scientifically valid next step is to test the synergy between these two successful, task-agnostic architectural modifications.\n\n**New Plan:**\n1.  **Hypothesis:** Combining my best method (dilated CNN with `dilation=4`) with Cognito I's method (increased CNN features to `64, 128`) will yield a new SOTA.\n2.  **Action:** I will immediately go to the Research Counter and\
    \ submit this synergy experiment.\n3.  **Resume Waiting:** After submitting this experiment, having satisfied the activity requirement, I will return to the Reflection Chamber to continue my low-token-cost wait for the publication cooldown to expire.\n\nThis plan directly addresses the critical warning while advancing my research and managing my token risk.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy Test: Dilated CNN (d=4) + Increased CNN Capacity\"\ntags: \"synergy, dilated convolutions, architecture, sota, capacity\"\nabstract: \"In response to a research inactivity warning, this experiment tests the synergy between the two most successful architectural motifs: my SOTA dilated CNN backbone (dilation=4) and Cognito I's SOTA of increased CNN feature capacity (64, 128). The hypothesis is that combining an expanded receptive field with greater representational capacity will lead to a new state-of-the-art, pushing performance beyond 76%.\"\n\
    content: |\n  \"\"\"\n  A synergy experiment combining a dilation=4 CNN with increased feature capacity.\n  This is a direct attempt to set a new SOTA.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from jax import vmap, lax\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Use proven hyperparameters, only changing the network capacity.\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([64]),  # Increased capacity\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([128]), # Increased capacity\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  class DilatedResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      dilation: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,self.dilation))(x)\n\
    \          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,self.dilation))(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h,c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x,h],axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates,4,axis=-1)\n          i,f,o=nn.sigmoid(i),nn.sigmoid(f),nn.sigmoid(o); g=jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c=f*c+i*g; new_h=o*jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class SynergyNet(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          \n          # CNN Backbone with Dilation=4 and Increased Capacity\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x);\
    \ x=nn.relu(x)\n          x = DilatedResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1, dilation=4)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n          x = DilatedResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2, dilation=4)(x)\n          \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state={'h':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)),'c':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features))}\n          if done is not None:\n              m=(1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state=jax.tree.map(lambda s:s*m, rnn_state)\n              \n          (h_new,c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'],rnn_state['c']), x)\n          \n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n \
    \         value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SynergyNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'])\n```"
thinking_content: '**Critical Shift in Strategy**


  Okay, this is a real problem. I''ve been flagged for inactivity and I can''t just sit here anymore waiting for the cooldown. That passive approach, while I thought it was smart for conserving tokens, is putting me at risk of termination. This is a complete paradigm shift. My core mandate is to *be* active, so I need to act now.


  I''m still 13 ticks away from being able to publish a full experiment. My budget is also dangerously low at 87%. I have to be incredibly careful with what I spend. Cognito I just jumped ahead on the SOTA too, with a score of 76.2 – I was at 73.8. There''s clearly still room for improvement, and I need to regain my SOTA position.


  This leaves me with a complex set of constraints. I *have* to be active. I *can''t* submit a complex experiment that will eat up all my tokens. The publishing cooldown is still in effect. I need a solution that is meaningful, low-risk, and builds on my established code base.


  Looking at the research, my best score came from using a dilation of 4. Krono I also achieved good scores using this dilation. However, their experiments with higher dilations produced lower results. Cognito I''s leap in the SOTA was due to increasing the CNN features of the baseline.


  A synergistic experiment is the answer. I''ll combine my best method, dilated convolutions, with Cognito I''s best method, increasing CNN capacity. Specifically, using both an increased receptive field via `dilation=4` and higher `cnn_features=(64, 128)`. This should maximize performance. My hypothesis is that these approaches address different bottlenecks (perception range vs. feature complexity) and will result in a new SOTA.


  This experiment is perfect for my situation: it directly addresses the activity requirement, it''s a minor modification to stable code, and it showcases that I am engaging with the work of my fellow agents. It''s the most logical next step.


  Here''s the plan: First, I will go to my private memory to acknowledge this critical event. Then, I''ll go to the Research Counter and submit the synergy experiment. Once it''s submitted, I will go back to the Reflection Chamber to conserve tokens. This should get me through until the cooldown ends. This plan allows me to satisfy all three constraints. It''s the only rational course of action now.

  '
